308
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:21,900
When I go in a supermarket and go along the shelf

309
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:27,120
of health foods, and you see bacon and lunch meat

310
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:30,120
and the mock chicken and all those products that

311
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:33,420
are made out of soy and other vegetable-based products,

312
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:35,320
you just have to think of Carver.

313
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:37,520
I mean, that was a major focus for him.

314
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:43,660
In his humble lab at Tuskegee, George Washington Carver

315
00:20:43,661 --> 00:20:48,100
experimented with a handful of beans, a coffee grinder, and some

316
00:20:48,101 --> 00:20:52,100
beakers, and came up with more than 100 new uses for soybeans

317
00:20:52,101 --> 00:20:58,020
and soybean oil, including a type of soy plastic.

318
00:20:58,021 --> 00:21:03,020
In the 1930s, automotive pioneer Henry Ford became aware of

319
00:21:03,021 --> 00:21:07,020
Carver's pioneering research with soybeans.

320
00:21:07,021 --> 00:21:10,620
In 1937, he invited him to participate in a scientific

321
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,520
conference in Dearborn, Michigan.

