00:27:36,901 --> 00:27:39,900
To achieve his brilliant blue color, Carver added a

421
00:27:39,901 --> 00:27:43,900
of potassium ferricyanide and nitric acid.

422
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:48,300
See, the genius of Carver was that he wouldn't just do that

423
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:51,640
and then write a paper and then get an award for doing that.

424
00:27:51,740 --> 00:27:56,140
He would then go out to people's farms

425
00:27:56,240 --> 00:28:00,460
and take these buckets of paint and stay overnight

426
00:28:00,560 --> 00:28:05,500
with the family, helping to paint and beautify their homes.

427
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:09,900
He was a chemist, a botanist, a biologist.

428
00:28:09,901 --> 00:28:14,740
an agronomist, and this consummate researcher.

429
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:19,040
George Washington Carver was a man way before his time.

430
00:28:19,140 --> 00:28:23,040
Can you imagine what he could have done with a computer?

431
00:28:23,140 --> 00:28:25,440
Carver was a fearless trailblazer,

432
00:28:25,540 --> 00:28:29,060
a driving force in discovering ways to use natural resources

433
00:28:29,160 --> 00:28:32,360
to benefit mankind.

434
00:28:32,460 --> 00:28:34,860
Another area of research he pioneered

