00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:37,900
is just now starting to give the oil industry

436
00:28:37,901 --> 00:28:39,400
A run for its money.

437
00:28:46,700 --> 00:28:49,360
We now return to George Washington Carver Tech

438
00:28:49,361 --> 00:28:50,660
on Modern Marvels.

439
00:28:54,840 --> 00:28:58,040
Today, American farmers are harvesting approximately 3

440
00:28:58,041 --> 00:29:00,540
billion bushels of soybeans per year.

441
00:29:04,640 --> 00:29:07,160
80% of the crop George Washington Carver

442
00:29:07,161 --> 00:29:10,160
championed is used for protein and food products for both

443
00:29:10,161 --> 00:29:18,160
human and animal consumption. The other 20% is used to

444
00:29:18,161 --> 00:29:22,160
produce soy oil, which, as Carver demonstrated, can be used

445
00:29:22,161 --> 00:29:29,160
for a variety of purposes. One of the fastest growing

446
00:29:29,161 --> 00:29:34,160
applications for the oil is in biodiesel technology.

447
00:29:34,161 --> 00:29:42,160
Biodiesel is a diesel fuel replacement that's made from any vegetable oil or animal fat.

448
00:29:42,161 --> 00:29:49,160
And the way that it's made is you take a vegetable oil and you react it with an alcohol like ethanol or methanol,

449
00:29:49,161 --> 00:29:58,160
and that reaction causes the glycerin to separate from the oil, and the resulting chemical compound is biodiesel.

450
00:29:58,161 --> 00:30:00,960
diesel, and it acts very chemically similar to diesel

451
00:30:00,961 --> 00:30:05,200
fuel in a diesel engine, except that it is 10 times less toxic

452
00:30:05,201 --> 00:30:09,400
than table salt and biodegrades as fast as sugar.

453
00:30:09,401 --> 00:30:13,600
The roots of biodiesel fuel go back to the 1930s, when Carver

454
00:30:13,601 --> 00:30:19,520
and Henry Ford recognized the need to find alternative fuels.

455
00:30:19,521 --> 00:30:22,520
With the economy facing a depression, they tried to turn

456
00:30:22,521 --> 00:30:25,520
the tide by applying more agricultural products to growing

457
00:30:25,521 --> 00:30:29,960
industrial markets, like plastics and rubber.

458
00:30:29,961 --> 00:30:34,860
Mr. Carver and Mr. Ford saw that the depletion of fossil

459
00:30:34,861 --> 00:30:39,700
fuels was inevitable. They looked for the use of plants,

460
00:30:39,701 --> 00:30:44,700
like soybeans, to be that fuel of the future.

461
00:30:44,701 --> 00:30:47,700
Carver and Ford believed that vegetable oils could be used to

462
00:30:47,701 --> 00:30:51,440
fuel internal combustion engines, and they were not alone in that

463
00:30:51,441 --> 00:30:55,520
conviction. Dr. Rudolph Diesel was a

464
00:30:55,521 --> 00:30:59,520
scientist who invented the first diesel engine.

465
00:30:59,521 --> 00:31:02,520
It's a compression ignition technology that's much more

466
00:31:02,521 --> 00:31:07,520
fuel efficient, and he ran that first engine on peanut oil.

467
00:31:07,521 --> 00:31:11,520
And he was a scientist along with George Washington Carver

468
00:31:11,521 --> 00:31:16,520
and Henry Ford, all scientists who had a vision for

469
00:31:16,521 --> 00:31:20,520
sustainability and renewable energy through agriculture.

470
00:31:20,521 --> 00:31:23,520
The high cost of agricultural energy sources

471
00:31:23,521 --> 00:31:29,020
